course: dictionary
lesson: 13440
title: Horticultural: words about growing plants
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Horticultural is a long, formal word, but its context gives you clues. It describes things to do with growing fruit, vegetables, flowers and garden plants. «The horticultural show had giant pumpkins and rows of red roses.» Pumpkins and roses are things grown in gardens, so horticultural must be about growing plants.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? In «She is studying horticultural science at college», the words science and college show a serious subject. Try the everyday word gardening in its place. The sentence still makes sense, so you know the meaning is close.
explain: Writers use horticultural in news, science and other formal writing. In everyday talk, people usually say gardening. When you see a long word like this, look for the plants, flowers or vegetables in the sentence. They will tell you the topic.
fact: Horticultural means having to do with growing fruit, vegetables, flowers and garden plants.
fact: Horticultural is a formal word, found in news, science and serious writing.
fact: A horticultural show is a show of flowers, plants and vegetables.
fact: A horticultural society is a club for people who grow plants.
exercise: «The horticultural show had giant pumpkins and rows of red roses.» What does horticultural mean here? | Having to do with swimming and sports | Having to do with cooking meals at home | Having to do with reading old books | *Having to do with growing plants and flowers
exercise: «She is studying horticultural science at college.» What is she learning about? | Stars and planets | How computers work | Old castles and kings | *Growing fruit, vegetables and garden plants
exercise: «The horticultural society met in the village hall to plan its spring flower display.» Find and copy one word that shows the topic is plants. | *flower | village | spring | society
test: Mia says horticultural means a kind of horse. What does it really mean? | Having to do with the sea and boats | Having to do with music and singing | Having to do with horses and riding | *Having to do with growing fruit, vegetables, flowers and garden plants
test: Which sentence uses horticultural correctly? | «My horticultural dog ran all the way to the park.» | «The horticultural team sang loudly in the street.» | *«The horticultural team planted apple trees along the path.»
exam: Zara asks, «Is horticultural mostly about growing plants or about building houses?» What is the answer? | Painting pictures | Cooking pasta | Building houses | *Growing plants
